export default "<p class=\"article-lead\">Only 14% of CFOs say they can clearly demonstrate the business impact of their AI investments. But among the 14% who are tracking it properly? 77% report a return of 2x or more. The problem isn't that AI doesn't work. The problem is that most organizations aren't measuring it.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>This Week in AI</h3>\n\n        <div class=\"ai-news-placeholder\">\n          <div class=\"ai-news-placeholder-icon\">\n            <svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z\"/></svg>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"ai-news-placeholder-text\">\n            <strong>This Week in AI</strong>\n            This section updates with the latest AI news each week, developments translated into plain business impact for leaders.\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <p>Now for this week's deep dive...</p>\n\n        <h3>The Silence That's Costing You</h3>\n\n        <p>Here's what's happening in boardrooms everywhere right now:</p>\n\n        <p>Someone presents an \"AI roadmap.\" There are slides. There's a timeline. There's enthusiasm. There may even be a live demo.</p>\n\n        <p>And then someone asks: \"What's the return?\"</p>\n\n        <p>Silence. Or worse, vague statements about \"long-term transformation\" and \"building capabilities for the future.\"</p>\n\n        <p><strong>That silence is costing your organization trust, budget, and competitive ground.</strong></p>\n\n        <p>The answer isn't to stop investing in AI. The answer is to start measuring it properly.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>The Context</h3>\n\n        <p>A 2024 McKinsey study found that <strong>35% of CEOs admit their AI projects create an \"illusion of progress\"</strong>, activity that looks like transformation but isn't producing measurable outcomes. The industry even has a name for it: <strong>AI washing</strong>.</p>\n\n        <p>It's not fraud. It's usually just a measurement gap.</p>\n\n        <p>The organizations pulling ahead are doing something remarkably simple: <strong>they defined success before they started.</strong></p>\n\n        <p>Three metrics. That's all it takes to begin.</p>\n\n        <p><strong>1. Time saved.</strong> How many hours per week does this AI capability return to your team? At what fully-loaded cost per hour? Multiply across the year.</p>\n\n        <p><strong>2. Quality improved.</strong> Is the output better? Are error rates down? Are customer satisfaction scores moving? Pick one measurable quality signal and track it.</p>\n\n        <p><strong>3. Cost reduced.</strong> What were you spending before, on tools, on people, on rework, on third parties? What are you spending now?</p>\n\n        <p>That's it. Not a framework. Not a six-month consulting engagement. Three lines on a spreadsheet, tracked every 30 days, with a 90-day target agreed up front.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>The Analogy</h3>\n\n        <p>Imagine you hire a marketing agency. They run campaigns for three months. At the quarterly review, you ask: \"Did this work?\"</p>\n\n        <p>They say: \"Oh, the team really learned a lot. We tested some new creative directions. The brand awareness is building. It's early days.\"</p>\n\n        <p>You'd fire them.</p>\n\n        <p>But in AI, we accept exactly this kind of non-answer, because \"it's new\" and \"it's complex\" and \"these things take time.\"</p>\n\n        <p><strong>They don't.</strong></p>\n\n        <p>Not when you set 90-day targets. Not when you define your three metrics on day one. Not when you treat AI investment like any other capital allocation decision.</p>\n\n        <p>A marketing campaign without conversion tracking isn't a campaign. It's an experiment with no hypothesis.</p>\n\n        <p><strong>AI without defined success metrics isn't a transformation. It's a budget line with a story attached.</strong></p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <div class=\"monks-story\">\n          <span class=\"monks-story-label\">Monks Success Story, Real AI ROI</span>\n          <p>Here's what measurement-first AI looks like in practice. These are numbers from actual campaigns Monks has run with clients.</p>\n          <p><strong>Headspace.</strong> AI-powered creative production at scale: 460 assets produced, two-thirds reduction in production time, 62% increase in conversion rate, 13% reduction in cost-per-signup. This work won \"Best Use of AI\" at the Drum Awards, the Digiday Awards, and the Meta Agency Awards.</p>\n          <p><strong>Hatch.</strong> 80% increase in click-through rate. 46% increase in engagement. 31% reduction in cost-per-acquisition.</p>\n          <p><strong>Amazon.</strong> 400% improvement in return on ad spend. 66% reduction in cost-per-acquisition.</p>\n          <p><strong>Forever 21.</strong> 66% ROI improvement.</p>\n          <p><strong>GM.</strong> Over 100 production-ready assets delivered in 18 days.</p>\n          <p>These aren't projections. They aren't pilots. They're client results, with before-and-after numbers, measured the same way you'd measure any other business investment.</p>\n          <p>Our co-founder Wesley ter Haar put it directly: <strong>\"An AI story that doesn't change economics isn't anything more than a story.\"</strong></p>\n          <p>We're moving toward <strong>subscription-based delivery models</strong>, where you pay for continuous AI capability, not individual projects. Our target: subscription pricing representing <strong>25% of our revenue by end of 2026</strong>. Why? Because it aligns our incentives with your results.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <blockquote>\n          <p>\"If your team says 'AI is going great' but can't show you a number, it's not going great. It's going nowhere.\"</p>\n        </blockquote>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <div class=\"action-callout\">\n          <div class=\"action-callout-label\">\n            <svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z\"/></svg>\n            Your One Action This Week\n          </div>\n          <p>Before your next AI budget conversation, whether you're approving spend, reviewing a vendor, or planning next quarter, do one thing:</p>\n          <p><strong>Define exactly three metrics you will track. Set a 90-day target for each. Write them down.</strong></p>\n          <p>Not \"we expect efficiency gains.\" Not \"we anticipate improved output quality.\"</p>\n          <p>Specific. Measurable. Time-bound.</p>\n          <p>Then hold the work to those numbers. Not in six months. In 90 days.</p>\n          <p><strong>That's how 14% becomes your number, and 2x becomes your floor.</strong></p>\n        </div>";
